7Cz", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 696120, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2. The worker is healthy again, but payments-api is still failing.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is on v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It now reports healthy, with errors down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 for payments-worker, and on-call has been paged. The first request timed out. I checked that no incident had been created, then retried with the same key so it couldn't be filed twice.\n- **Still broken:** payments-api is still on v5.1.0, unhealthy at 18% errors. It may just be catching up, but its own deploy history marks v5.1.0 as \"degraded,\" so the API release could be a separate problem. I put this in the incident summary.\n\nIf payments-api doesn't recover in the next few minutes, I can roll it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release. I won't do that unless you say so.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01F2kXmHkczR2aKwL5dXy2hU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CtZXaNy4AVYwzWSBbnpyiY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01FqrTD6shnhBf7zpbhhpnfZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.7}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01X45B1rw5fhntXvmS6pkTRY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.6},